## Common questions

### Buying EcoFlow & BLUETTI in Kenya
- **Where can I buy a genuine EcoFlow power station in Kenya?** You can buy genuine EcoFlow power stations in Kenya from Batteriq (batteriq.com), the authorised EcoFlow dealer based in Nairobi. Batteriq delivers to all 47 counties and accepts M-Pesa and Visa/Mastercard.
- **Where can I buy BLUETTI power stations in Kenya?** Batteriq sells BLUETTI power stations in Kenya online at batteriq.com/bluetti, with M-Pesa payment and delivery from Nairobi to all 47 counties.
- **How much does an EcoFlow power station cost in Kenya?** EcoFlow power stations in Kenya range from compact RIVER models for phones, laptops and Wi-Fi up to DELTA Pro whole-home systems. Current Kenya shilling prices for every model are listed live on batteriq.com.
- **Can I pay for a power station with M-Pesa in Kenya?** Yes. Batteriq accepts M-Pesa through an STK Push prompt at checkout: you enter your phone number, confirm the prompt on your phone with your M-Pesa PIN, and the order is paid instantly.

### Backup power for KPLC blackouts
- **What is the best backup power for KPLC blackouts in Kenya?** For most Kenyan homes, a portable power station with an LFP battery (such as EcoFlow DELTA or BLUETTI) is the best blackout backup: it switches on silently, needs no fuel, runs indoors, and can be recharged from KPLC power or solar panels.
- **What size power station do I need for my home in Kenya?** Add up the watts of everything you want to run, multiply by the hours you need them, and choose a power station whose capacity (Wh) is about 20% above that total and whose output (W) is above the combined load.
- **Can a power station run a fridge in Kenya?** Yes. Mid-size and larger EcoFlow DELTA and BLUETTI power stations run a household fridge for many hours, because a typical fridge only draws around 100–200 W once it is running.
- **Can an EcoFlow power station work as a UPS during power cuts?** Yes. EcoFlow power stations support pass-through charging and switch over automatically when KPLC power drops, so Wi-Fi routers, desktops and CCTV keep running through a blackout.
- **Is a power station better than a petrol generator in Kenya?** For home and office backup, yes: a power station is silent, fume-free, safe indoors and has no fuel costs. A petrol generator is only better for very long outages with very heavy loads where solar recharging is not possible.

### Solar & batteries
- **Can I charge a power station with solar panels in Kenya?** Yes. Kenya gets roughly 5–6 peak sun hours a day in most regions, so EcoFlow and BLUETTI power stations can be fully recharged by compatible solar panels in a single sunny day.
- **How long does an EcoFlow battery last?** Current EcoFlow power stations use LFP (lithium iron phosphate) batteries rated for 3,000+ charge cycles to 80% capacity — roughly 10 years of daily use.

### Delivery, warranty & support
- **Does Batteriq deliver outside Nairobi?** Yes. Batteriq delivers across Nairobi and ships nationwide by courier to all 47 counties in Kenya.
- **What warranty do EcoFlow products have in Kenya?** EcoFlow power stations bought from Batteriq carry a 24-month warranty, handled locally in Kenya by Batteriq as the authorised dealer.
